cles which are faster and more  mobile and more agile and so they've  gone for Speed in this offensive and it  seems to have paid off using Western  methods Western training and quite a lot  of Western Equipment  this offensive has exposed the fragility  the brittleness of Russia's military  Machinery because their troops are not  especially well motivated they don't  seem to be very well trained or very  well supplied and the speed at which  they have collapsed they haven't just  withdrawn they have collapsed the  officer seems to too many officers seem  to run away and when the officer runs  away the men just disappear why should  they stay if the officer is not prepared  to to stay and take risks and the as we  were years of neglect of Russian forces  have become pretty clear and it isn't  just the scratch forces who seem to have  disintegrated the first guards tank Army  seems to have disintegrated the first  guard's tank arm is one of their elite  units it's one of their best units and  yet it's it seemed to withdrawn in a  hurry leaving most of its tanks behind  if if a guard's tank regiment doesn't  have its tanks it doesn't have anything  um it's the same seems to happen to the  fourth guards tank regiment and so this  has been a real humiliation not just for  the militias and the chechens and the  Wagner  private military companies who are  working for the Russians this has been  humiliation to some of the elite  regiments of the Russian army and they  haven't had anything as bad as this on  an open Battlefield they haven't lost on  an open Battlefield like this since  December 1942.  I don't think it's true to say that the  operation in the southwest in Kirsten  was all a decoy to draw Russian forces  away from the parking region although it  did have that effect all the evidence is  that the ukrainians fully intend to  conduct a true prong defensive and that  is indeed what they're doing the New  York Times has recently reported that  this offensive this 