y to go for liberating more  territory in the dombas or even more  territory further south somewhere south  of zaparisia even as far down as marupol  or litepol on the coast they get to  choose  for the Russians what happens next is  that they have to buy time they're going  backwards there's no natural line that  they can stop at so they need to dig in  somewhere and wait for the winter  and then what happens next is that there  will almost certainly be a major  strategic offensive by the Russians  probably early next year and that may be  another big turning point in the war one  thing we're all certain about is that  President Putin will not be giving up  although he can't do very much about  these Battlefield losses in the short  term he will try to keep Ukraine Under  Pressure probably by attacking the  civilian population by attacking the  critical National infrastructure Maybe  by a series of cyber attacks he will up  the ante for what this whole war is  about and undoubtedly he will try to do  something that takes Everybody by  surprise and so he'll respond to this  battlefield reversal not by giving up  but by actually taking the war in a  different direction and both Ukraine and  the Western backers of Ukraine will have  to be ready
 

